From: terbin <terbin.2b2t@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Upgrade chunks post-spin

After initServer has returned and one-tick init tasks have run, but
before the main tick loop opens, check whether --upgradeChunks was
requested. If so, dispatch ChunkUpgrader.run, mark the phase complete,
and halt the server cleanly. The default backend is parallel direct-NBT
(DirectNbtUpgrader): workers each own one region file and DFU chunk NBT
in place via SimpleRegionStorage.upgradeChunkTag, with no chunk-system
involvement. With --normalize, the chunk-system load-and-save path runs
instead, with a pre-pass snapshot and post-pass fringe cleanup. See
docs/upgrade-via-direct-nbt-plan.md and
docs/upgrade-via-chunk-system-plan.md for rationale.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java b/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
index 440e5d2c199c6e8cbab2d5c92256cccfd0c555fe..46dc698df7c37c7b39f27b211b1a544073eb0c17 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
@@ -1336,6 +1336,15 @@ public abstract class MinecraftServer extends ReentrantBlockableEventLoop<TickTa
                 CompletableFuture.runAsync(com.destroystokyo.paper.PaperVersionFetcher::getUpdateStatusStartupMessage, io.papermc.paper.util.MCUtil.ASYNC_EXECUTOR);
             }
             // Paper end - Improve outdated version checking
+            // The Archive start - upgrade chunks post-spin
+            if (archive.ArchiveSettings.upgradeChunksRequested()
+                    && !archive.ArchiveSettings.upgradeChunksComplete()) {
+                archive.ChunkUpgrader.run(this);
+                archive.ArchiveSettings.markUpgradeChunksComplete();
+                this.halt(false);
+                return;
+            }
+            // The Archive end - upgrade chunks post-spin

             while (this.running) {
                 final long tickStart = System.nanoTime(); // Paper - improve tick loop
